version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24136905
repository-code: https://github.com/1956178912/AITester
abstract: >-
  A Python system for attribution-aware evaluation of LLM-based unit test
  generation and repair. The current evaluation batch spans two endpoints
  (deepseek-flash and mimo-v2.6-pro), five baseline arms and five benchmarks.
  Every declared pass is adjudicated against held-out gold material, so pass
  rates are reported together with a false-fix rate; the harness records
  exclusions explicitly, and generation-stage costs stay in the record.
  Detection-first prompting, held-out gold adjudication and paired reporting
  keep the measurement auditable, with multi-agent orchestration included as
  an ablatable container rather than a primary claim. The version-locked
  derived verdict rows and 50-cell aggregates are archived under DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.24136905; the implementation and zero-LLM recomputation
  chain are in this repository.
keywords:
  - software testing
  - LLM agents
  - unit test generation
  - automated program repair
  - false fixes
  - measurement validity
  - benchmark evaluation
